# `orderby`: DS0104 pointing at `sort by`, with a fix.
mode: syntax
---- query
'orders.csv' | orderby amount desc
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..35
  PIPELINE@0..34
    LITERAL@0..12
      STRING@0..12 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@12..13 " "
    PIPE@13..14 "|"
    WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
    SORT_OP@15..34
      IDENT@15..22 "orderby"
      WHITESPACE@22..23 " "
      SORT_KEY@23..34
        NAME_REF@23..29
          IDENT@23..29 "amount"
        WHITESPACE@29..30 " "
        IDENT@30..34 "desc"
  WHITESPACE@34..35 "\n"

error[DS0104]: unknown operator `orderby`
  --> query:1:16
  |
1 | 'orders.csv' | orderby amount desc
  |                ^^^^^^^ not a DataScript operator
  |
  = help: to sort rows, use `sort by`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    'orders.csv' | sort by amount desc
which parses without errors
